WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.388 --> 00:00:02.971
(upbeat music)

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:09.284
[Derek] Hey Rob, This is
Derek from Chico, California,

00:00:09.284 --> 00:00:11.260
and I love the pod.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:13.290
One thing I don't think
you've talked about much is

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:16.750
where you've traveled in your
life, not that I recall anyway

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:20.100
What is the most
unexpectedly wonderful place

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:23.214
you've ever traveled to in the world,

00:00:23.214 --> 00:00:26.640
and where would you like to
go that you haven't been?

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:27.473
Thanks for answering.

00:00:27.473 --> 00:00:30.793
Thank you, Derek for
calling, the Lowe Down Line.

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:35.110
I don't know how unexpected
it is, but without a doubt

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:39.520
the place that when I landed
there and looked at it,

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:42.310
I was just moved almost tears by,

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:44.690
was the Island of Bora Bora.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:49.654
It is absolutely magical beyond belief.

00:00:49.654 --> 00:00:52.770
The other place was surprising

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:54.950
because you hear about Yosemite,

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:55.840
I live in California,

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:58.410
I've lived, You're in Chico,
you're in California as well

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:02.650
and I finally got to Yosemite
and I came around the corner

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:04.540
and looked at that
Yosemite Valley and my eyes

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:07.350
just spilled over with tears.

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:09.840
It is, the Yosemite Valley,

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:12.633
if you traveled across
the world to get there,

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:15.840
you wouldn't have been disappointed

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:19.500
and yet it's right in my state
and I'd never gotten there.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.970
Just beyond spectacular.

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:23.940
Where would I like to go?

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:25.870
Well, you know where I wanna go?

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:29.810
I wanna go to Japan, to ski.

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:30.720
That's what I wanna do.

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:33.380
There's and I should know
the name of it, but I don't,

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:35.930
but there's a resort on,

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:37.543
I think it's the Island of Hokkaido,

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:40.000
I hope I'm pronouncing it right,

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:43.350
that has the most powder
of anywhere in the world

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:45.440
and skiing connoisseurs know

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:47.340
that that is the place you go for powder.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:51.080
So the notion of having like
amazing authentic Japanese food

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:56.080
and powdered ski every
day is next literally,

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:57.313
next on my bucket list.

00:01:57.313 --> 00:01:59.896
(upbeat music)

